**3 [[Bore]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Angelic Gories and Bores are usually easy enough to manage using damage alone, but not when they team up in massive swarms. Tanking is out of the equation with their extreme DPS, so abuse CC units as much as possible. The very general go-to you should do is to stall for money before hitting the base. Then, the next step is to stop the [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] quickly before more spawn and interrupt your frontline.

CC effects are much more important in higher difficulties, as in {{3c}} the Angelic Gories will deal upwards of '''62k DPS''' and the Bores will deal more than '''100k DPS''', disintegrating everything they touch, to the point where Stone Cat can actually perish.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: Stone Cat can tank the extreme DPS of the enemies in this stage without a sweat. On higher-crown difficulties, {{3c}} especially, leveling them up to 50 is highly encouraged for the extra bulk.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Ramen Cat is an obvious choice on a stage with high DPS Angels, but doesn't work quite as well as usual without something to crowd-control the Bores.
*Talented [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]: His spammability, low cooldown and most importantly, Area Attack make him quite crucial if you lack other good anti-Angel Crowd-Controllers for the Angelic Gories.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: Her combination of damage, survivability and spammability make her a very effective unit on this stage, even in {{3c}}. Purchasing her Survive [[Talents|Talent]] to ensure she lives an extra hit is strongly recommended.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Cyberpunk's high range and long Slow make them a great crowd-controller for this stage. Beware that the enemies will push into their blind spot eventually, so either stacking several of them at the start or bringing support is encouraged.
*[[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]]: While Bubble Cat likely won't be available on {{1c}} due to the difficulty of unlocking it, Bubble Cat can be a great help for {{2c}} and beyond, since its piercing range allows it to hit the Angels from behind the Bores, though do note its large blindspot can be a hindrance if not protected properly.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can is obviously effective for getting Extra Money from the peons when Talented, but their Slow ability can also see some use here in nullifying the extreme pushing power of the Bores. Their high health also lets them survive a hit or two, even on higher crowns, though Single Target makes them ineffective for killing crowds when they stack up.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]]: Doron's foreswing and extreme tankiness can give your units some breathing room while he's alive. His [[True Form]] isn't necessary for him to work either, since this stage contains no Colossus, Behemoth or Relic enemies. Note that he also won't be available on the first run through, due to being unlocked later on in Uncanny Legends. Do note that if enemies push too hard into Doron, he can die due to higher difficulties ramping magnifications to high degrees.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: Thanks to their [[Massive Damage]] VS Angel enemies, as well as their high range Area Attacks, Mushroom Cat is perfectly-suited for dealing with almost every enemy in this stage. Be sure to protect them well, because they won't survive an attack from any enemy on higher crown difficulties.
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcrates]]: If you're planning to do this on higher difficulties, it is recommended to use Catcractes, as his high attack rate, DPS, Omni-Strike, Conjure and Freeze makes him a potent unit to bring into this battle, especially if you don't have Ubers that can make the stage easier.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Momotaro]]: Momotaro's very short recharge coupled with their 30% chance to freeze Red and Angels with 100% uptime means they absolutely destroy this stage, as with a fair bit of luck they can form a stack and perma-freeze everything, prevailing even in {{3c}}.
*[[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]]: Mitama's [[Long Distance]] [[Slow]] effect proves to be especially useful against the hyperbuffed Angelic Gories and Bore. [[Resistant]] VS traited also ensures she doesn't get instantly killed by them too.
*[[Juvens (Uber Rare Cat)|Holiday Juvens CC]]: If you happen to own him, Juvens is an amazing meatshield which can soak up attacks from every Angel enemy here—provided you can keep the Bore in check. His fast recharge time also makes him easier to replace when lost.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultima Galaxy Cosmo]]: Cosmo's long foreswing can be turned into an advantage here, since the ridiculous pushing power of the enemies will cause them to run right into his attack range to be frozen. His [[Ultra Form]] only improves him more, effectively doubling his damage and extending his reach massively thanks to his [[Wave Attack]].
*[[Wonder MOMOCO (Legend Rare Cat)|Wonder MOMOCO]]: While she is mostly inferior to Momotaro due to having much worse uptime, she can be a serviceable replacement if you own her but not Momotaro. Her Wave Attack also means she can freeze the whole field instead of just the frontline, unlike Momotaro.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Doom Phono]]: Phono essentially acts like a lower-ranged Cyberpunk, who trades standing range for larger area coverage and mini surges that slow everything that touch them for a couple seconds. Although he has a bit of downtime, he synergizes very well with other crowd control units that can cover his downtime, like [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] or [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet]].

==Trivia==
*''Palcaccio'' is not an actual word in any language, but in Japanese it sounds almost the same as ''carpaccio'' (''carpaccio'' is ''karupatcho'', ''palcaccio'' is ''parukatcho'').

